    <string name="lesson_length">Length conversions use the meter as the SI base. Multiply by a fixed factor to reach meters, then divide by the target unit’s factor. A mile is exactly 1,609.344 meters.</string>
    <string name="lesson_mass">Mass conversions use the kilogram. Imperial units are defined exactly: 1 pound is 0.45359237 kg, and 1 ounce is 1/16 of a pound.</string>
    <string name="lesson_temperature">Temperature is not a simple scale factor. Convert through Celsius: F = C × 9/5 + 32, and K = C + 273.15. Absolute zero is 0 K (−273.15 °C).</string>
    <string name="lesson_volume">Volume conversions use the liter (0.001 m³). A US liquid gallon is exactly 3.785411784 liters. 1 milliliter equals 1 cubic centimeter.</string>
    <string name="lesson_area">Area conversions use the square meter. An acre is 4,046.8564224 m², and a hectare is 10,000 m² (a 100 m × 100 m square).</string>
    <string name="lesson_speed">Speed conversions use meters per second. Divide km/h by 3.6 to get m/s. A knot is one nautical mile (1,852 m) per hour.</string>

